From da1a3a8443b75f15d86c776e654abeb65ae0fea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:21:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): chat links synced through the Board (RFC phase
 5) [daveey]

Which chats a card belongs to becomes a synced table, task_chat_links (card,
chat gateway/profile/session, kind created|shepherd, released), so every
gateway's replica can answer a chat's cards on every gateway.

- kanban_chat_links.reconcile (sync loop, every 60 s per synced board; its
  first run is the backfill) writes this gateway's links: creating chats
  (tasks.session_id), shepherd subscriptions (tui notify subs) and this
  gateway's chats' links to other gateways' cards from the origin-ledger
  projection with their released state. Missing links are released, never
  deleted. Writes go through the capture triggers like any synced row.
- replica_cards answers a lineage's open remote cards from the replicas;
  session_tasks uses it when kanban.sync.links_reader is 'replica' (default
  stays the origin ledger).
- hermes kanban sync links (reconcile now) and links-diff (ledger vs replica
  per chat; exit 1 when not clean): readers switch only once it is clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
